    {
      "post_id": "87011",
      "author_handle": "jhay",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "It is fine to lift after a C-Section as long as you wear a binder. In other places, they would really encourage you to do so but with a limit. Wearing a binder would definitely help a lot. It prevents tearing of the operations that would cause bleeding and opening of wounds.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9660/#87011",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/7dbfafb4d3e421f2da5f.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9660/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "85259"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "87013",
      "author_handle": "morgoodie",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "I had C-sections with both of my children. I did not do any lifting other than them after I had the surgeries. I never had any problems with the incisions. I had staples and tape instead of sutures so I do not know if that made it any better. The area around the incision has no feeling and it feels weird sometimes but does not bother me. I have heard of these binders but have never used one. I hear they work really well.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9660/#87013",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/7dbfafb4d3e421f2da5f.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9660/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "85259"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "87028",
      "author_handle": "jhay",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "Yup.. it really helped a lot. but of course you're not going to lift things more than the weight of your new baby.. Oh good for you you have staples.. we only have stitches so.. yup its better to have the binder.",
